*yarn.lock
# Exception: commit the Kotlin/JS lockfiles for reproducible CI builds.
# Without them, CI must freshly resolve/generate yarn.lock every run, and
# that fresh-generation path was observed to fail on windows-latest runners
# (kotlinStoreYarnLock / kotlinWasmStoreYarnLock: "Input file does not
# exist") even though it worked on ubuntu-latest. Restoring from a known-
# good committed lockfile avoids the fresh-generation path entirely.
!kotlin-js-store/**/yarn.lock
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
*.log
.vscode/
node_modules/
supabase/.branches/
supabase/.temp/
/release.bat
/androidApp/release/
